window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"zaahen","b":"masteryi","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Skill","Master Yi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your engine starts first: E Golden Onslaught reaches him and the Q-E trade beats his single Alpha Strike - commit on every wave he steps up to."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Keep the boot down: glaive poke taxes his farm and your bruiser stats win every commit - each kill or plate here buys insurance against his late game."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R heals off the damage dealt, it does not hold him - the tool that stops him is your W pull, and any CC cancels Meditate outright. Highlander is 85s."},{"when":"2 items","text":"Wuju Style (14s) is the true damage, not Double Strike, and at two items it out-duels your rotation - stop side-laning him and fight him only where your team finishes it."}],"wants":{"you":["Q-E commits on his itemless levels","A lead banked before his true-damage core","W pull landed before Highlander starts rolling"],"foe":["Meditate healing him through your prime","Alpha Strike untargetable through burst","Late duels where resets outlast your drain"]},"early":"Level 1 is mutual farming with no all-in tools online, then the lane is yours: at 2 your E crosses the gap and the trade beats a kit whose only answer is one Alpha Strike on 20s, and at 3 the full Q-W-E rotation bursts him while the W pull drags him back out of that exit - commit early and often.","mid":"Levels 4-5 keep you firmly ahead - your Q taxes his farm and your bruiser stats win every straight commit, so convert the pressure into kills and plates now. At 6 it evens: Alpha Strike is 20s at rank 1 but his own autos cut it down, and Highlander (85s) makes him immune to slows, so open the fight with your W pull and not with your R, which only heals.","late":"His first item pulls the duel even - his DPS spikes while the heals on your Q and R hold the line - and two items in Wuju Style's true damage out-duels your rotation outright. Buy Grievous Wounds for Meditate, bank your early lead, and late game save the W pull for the moment he commits so your carries can erase him.","whys":["Level 1 is even farm - no all-in tools online for either side.","Level 2 is yours: E Golden Onslaught reaches him and your Q-E trade beats his single Alpha Strike.","Level 3 stays yours - Q-W-E bursts him, and your W pull drags him back out of an Alpha Strike exit.","Levels 4-5 keep you ahead as glaive poke taxes his farm and your bruiser stats win every commit.","Level 6 is even - Highlander is 85s and immune to slows, and your R heals rather than holds him.","His first item spikes his DPS but your Q and R heals hold the duel even.","Two-plus items his Wuju Style true damage out-duels your rotation outright."]});
